# Frontend configuration.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to client code. Anything you put
# here ships inside the JavaScript bundle — never put secrets, API keys or tokens
# in this file.

# Backend origin.
#
# In development this is the target of the Vite dev-server proxy (vite.config.ts),
# so the browser only ever talks to http://localhost:5173 and /api/* is forwarded
# here. It must be an absolute URL for the proxy to accept it.
#
# In a production build the proxy does not exist — the SPA is served behind nginx,
# which routes /api to the backend. The Docker build passes VITE_API_URL=/api so
# that client code reading `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL` gets a same-origin path.
#
# Note: no component reads this yet — the template ships without an API client.
# When you add one, read it as `import.meta.env.VITE_API_URL`.
#
# Default if unset: http://localhost:3000
VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
